{
  "slug": "craft-statusline",
  "name": "Craft Statusline",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A Claude Code statusline written in bash. Shows model and effort level, a state-aware git branch badge, context window with absolute-token traffic light (yellow at 400k tokens, red at 85%), rolling 5h and 7d rate limits, and optional session cost. Zero Node, zero Python, zero Nerd Fonts. Only requires jq. Bash 3.2 compatible, runs on macOS, Linux, and WSL.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **5 commands**.\n\n- **Commands** (5): `install` (Wire craft-statusline into ~/.claude/settings.json so Claude Code renders it), `off` (Disable a craft-statusline field), `on` (Enable a craft-statusline field), `status` (Show current craft-statusline configuration and a live render preview), `uninstall` (Remove craft-statusline from ~/.claude/settings.json (does not uninstall the plugin itself))\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install craft-statusline@claude-community` from `derjochenmeyer/claude-code-craft-statusline`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "command",
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
